  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that the sum of the interior angles of a polygon with $n$ sides is ${180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2).$\n\nTo find the number of sides in our polygon, we start by setting up the following equation:\n\n$$\n{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2)=1\\,{260}^{∘}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $n,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & =1\\,{260}^{∘} \\\\ n-2 & =\\frac{1\\,{260}^{∘}}{{180}^{∘}} \\\\ n-2 & =7 \\\\ n & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polygon has $n=9$ sides (so it is a nonagon).",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
